<!--
Blitzy skin verification fixture. harness/provision.sh authors this page with core's
maintenance/edit.php, which takes the title as its positional argument and reads the content
from standard input:

    php maintenance/edit.php 'Category:Blitzy verification fixtures' \
        --user "$BLITZY_TEST_USER" \
        --summary 'Blitzy fixture: verification category description' \
        < skins/Blitzy/fixtures/category-page.wikitext

The provisioning contract, recorded here so that it travels with the file:

* The target title is exactly "Category:Blitzy verification fixtures", byte-identical to the
  category link carried by fixtures/main-page.wikitext and fixtures/talk-page.wikitext. One
  character of difference in case or spacing would quietly create a second, empty category,
  and the category capture would show an empty listing instead of the member pages.
* Do NOT pass --createonly. maintenance/edit.php stops with "Page already exists" when the
  page is there already, whereas a plain re-save of identical content is a null edit that
  stores no new revision, so re-provisioning this page stays safe and repeatable.
* --user must be BLITZY_TEST_USER, the ordinary preferences-populated account, and never
  MW_ADMIN_USER, because no capture may display the administrator name.
* Only the description below is authored here. Core's CategoryViewer builds the listing
  beneath it, the mw-pages region and the generated mw-category lists, from the category
  links on the member pages: never list members by hand, and never wrap or restyle that
  region. Its chrome belongs to skinStyles/mediawiki.special.less, and the category links it
  is built from to resources/skins.blitzy.styles/components/Footer.less.
* The wikitext below is fixed on purpose: no signature tildes, no style attribute, nothing
  the pre-save transform can expand, and no magic word that varies with the clock, the site
  or the size of the member set. edit.php saves through PageUpdater, and
  DerivedPageDataUpdater::prepareContent() applies preSaveTransform, so anything expandable
  would be rewritten at provision time and consecutive capture runs would stop being
  byte-identical.
* This page carries no category and no behaviour switch of its own. A category link back to
  itself would make the category its own subcategory, and hiding the category would strip it
  from the catlinks footer of every member page, which is the surface the skin styles as pill
  chips.
-->
This category collects the pages that are authored by hand for the '''Blitzy''' skin's
verification harness, as distinct from the reference articles that are imported from
Wikipedia. Grouping them keeps the locally written content identifiable, and it gives the
harness one page whose listing is known before a run begins.

Membership is deliberately narrow, and it is declared by the committed wikitext fixtures
themselves rather than added afterwards. The imported articles keep the categories they
arrived with and are never placed here, and nothing in this description or in the pages it
collects is generated at view time, so the listing below reads the same on every run.
